<%#
Cistergraphia: the plate (fol. 2r)
==================================

Purpose:
- Show the generated Cistergraphia and let the user keep it

Design Decisions:
- The SVG is shown on the leaf in ink colours (CSS only); exports stay the
  plain black-on-white file that the decoder reads
- Strokes are inked in reading order and dry from rubric to ink (JS), so the
  snail is visible; the plate can be walked sign by sign (pointer or arrow keys)
- "Read it back" posts the same SVG to /decode: a one-click round trip
- Rongorongo plates can be turned half round (JS, CSS only): the turned rows
  then read upright, as the readers of Rapa Nui turned their tablets
- A grille's plate shows its key, and its grille: the stencil (the server's,
  embedded once) is laid over the plate and turned N, E, S, W, lighting the
  signs under its holes; the same file downloads, to print and cut. The key
  goes along with "Read it back"
- A weathered plate shows its lacunae; walking a worn sign says it is worn,
  never its value (the page must not hold the answer)
- The restoration bench (weathered plates): choose a lacuna on the plate or
  step through them, press a digit back in, and the pair is weighed. The page
  only knows what the file shows, so it says whether pairs balance, never
  whether a restoration is right: the words, and Read it back, decide. Its
  first state is drawn by the server, so nothing moves when the script arrives
- A broken plate shows its board and, below it, the tray of fragments. With
  the script, the fragments move: drag one, or pick it and then a cell of
  the board for its top-left corner; arrow keys move a picked fragment by a
  cell, T or a double click turns it half round. Once they cover the board,
  the page weighs every pair along both reading paths, and says how many
  balance. The page holds what the file shows, never where a fragment goes.
  A weathered broken plate is weighed by what each worn sign may hold; whole
  again, it reads as an edition (there is no bench on a plate in pieces)
- Nothing moves while you walk or turn the plate: the live reading takes the
  resting caption's place, and the script-only controls have their space from
  the first paint

Constraints:
- Copy/download need JS; the inline SVG can always be saved from the page
%>
<section class="leaf" aria-labelledby="plate-title">
  <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 2<sup>r</sup></p>
  <h1 id="plate-title" class="rubric"><%= @secret ? 'Your sealed Cistergraphia' : 'Your Cistergraphia' %></h1>

  <p class="message-echo"><span class="visually-hidden">Message: </span><q><%= @message %></q></p>
  <% if @decoy %>
    <p class="decoy-echo"><span class="label">For the novice</span> <q><%= @decoy %></q></p>
  <% end %>
  <% if @pieces && @damage %>
    <p class="lede">Broken and weathered: <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %>, <%= @damage.size %> <%= @damage.size == 1 ? 'lacuna' : 'lacunae' %>. Rejoin them on the board: a join is right when every pair can balance, whatever its lacunae held. Whole again, the plate reads as an edition. Read it back to have the decoder do both.</p>
  <% elsif @pieces %>
    <p class="lede">Broken: <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %>. Rejoin them on the board: a join is right when every pair of signs balances again. Read it back to have the decoder rejoin them.</p>
  <% elsif @damage %>
    <p class="lede">Weathered: <%= @damage.size %> <%= @damage.size == 1 ? 'lacuna' : 'lacunae' %>. Restore what is lost: each pair of signs must sum to a value on the tablet. Read it back to see the edition.</p>
  <% elsif @secret %>
    <p class="lede">Secret mode: sealed with your passphrase. Without it, this plate reveals nothing but its length.</p>
  <% elsif @normalized != @message %>
    <p class="lede">Enciphered as: <code><%= @normalized %></code></p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="lede">A game: anyone patient enough can read it back.</p>
  <% end %>

  <dl class="specs">
    <div><dt>Mode</dt><dd><%= @secret ? 'Secret' : 'Game' %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Signs</dt><dd><%= @symbols %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Grid</dt><dd><%= Integer.sqrt(@symbols) %> × <%= Integer.sqrt(@symbols) %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Layout</dt><dd><%= layout_name(@layout) %></dd></div>
    <% if @pieces %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Broken, in <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %><%= ', and weathered' if @damage %></dd></div>
    <% elsif @damage || @tally %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd><%= [('Weathered' if @damage), ('tally signs' if @tally)].compact.join(', with ').capitalize %></dd></div>
    <% end %>
    <% if grille? && @decoy %>
      <div><dt>Abbot’s key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout %></code></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Novice’s key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout.novice %></code></dd></div>
    <% elsif grille? %>
      <div><dt>Grille key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout %></code></dd></div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>

  <% if @pieces %>
  <figure class="plate plate--broken">
    <div class="plate-frame" id="svg-display" data-plate role="group"
         aria-label="The broken plate: an empty board, and below it the tray of fragments, some turned half round."
         data-fragments="<%= fragments_json(@svg_content, Integer.sqrt(@symbols)) %>">
      <%== @svg_content %>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="plate-reading"><span class="plate-reading-rest">The board above, the fragments below. Their edges are worn: only the sums show where each one goes.</span></span>
      <span class="plate-hint awaits-script" data-plate-hint>Drag a fragment onto the board, or pick it and then the cell for its top-left corner. Arrow keys move a picked fragment; T or a double click turns it. Turn and swap them until every pair balances.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="rejoin awaits-script" aria-labelledby="rejoin-title" data-rejoin>
    <div class="rejoin-head">
      <h2 id="rejoin-title" class="index-heading">Rejoin it</h2>
      <div class="rejoin-tools">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-rejoin-turn disabled>Turn half round</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-rejoin-reset>Back to the tray</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="rejoin-status" data-rejoin-status aria-live="polite">On the board: 0 of <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %>.</p>
    <p class="rejoin-reading" data-rejoin-reading aria-live="polite"></p>
  </section>
  <% else %>
  <figure class="plate">
    <div class="plate-frame" id="svg-display" data-plate tabindex="0" role="group"
         aria-label="The plate. Use the arrow keys to walk its signs in reading order."
         data-plate-cells="<%= plate_cells_json(@sequence, @layout, @damage || {}) %>" data-plate-layout="<%= plate_layout_json(@sequence, @layout) %>">
      <%== @svg_content %>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="plate-reading">
        <% if @layout == :rongorongo %>
          <span class="plate-reading-rest">Read from the bottom left, left to right; turn the plate half round for each next line.</span>
        <% elsif grille? && @decoy %>
          <span class="plate-reading-rest">Two grilles share this plate: the abbot’s reads the message, the novice’s the other one. The abbot’s key gives both; the novice’s, only its own.</span>
        <% elsif grille? %>
          <span class="plate-reading-rest">Read through the grille: N at the top, the holes row by row, then a quarter turn clockwise. Without it, the plate is an anagram of itself.</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="plate-reading-rest">Read clockwise from the top-left corner, coiling inward.</span>
        <% end %>
        <span class="plate-reading-live" data-plate-reading aria-live="polite"></span>
      </span>
      <span class="plate-hint awaits-script" data-plate-hint>Point at a sign, or focus the plate and use the arrow keys, to walk it in reading order.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <% end %>

  <% if @damage && !@pieces %>
    <% entries = lacunae(@sequence, @layout, @damage) %>
    <% first = entries.first %>
    <section class="bench awaits-script" aria-labelledby="bench-title" data-bench
             data-lacunae="<%= JSON.generate(entries) %>" data-glyph-table="<%= glyph_table_json %>"<% if @tally %>
             data-tally="<%= JSON.generate(Cistergraphia::Tally.signs(@sequence, @layout)) %>"<% end %>>
      <div class="bench-head">
        <h2 id="bench-title" class="index-heading">Restore it</h2>
        <div class="bench-nav">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-bench-step="-1" aria-label="Previous lacuna">‹</button>
          <span class="bench-which" data-bench-which aria-live="polite">Lacuna 1 of <%= entries.size %>: the <%= place_name(first[:place]) %></span>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--small" data-bench-step="1" aria-label="Next lacuna">›</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bench-palette" role="group" aria-label="Digits to press into the lacuna">
        <% 10.times do |digit| %>
          <button type="button" class="bench-digit" data-digit="<%= digit %>" aria-pressed="false"<%= ' disabled' unless first[:digits].include?(digit) %>>
            <%== glyph_svg(digit * first[:place], css: 'glyph bench-glyph', title: "#{digit} in the #{place_name(first[:place])}") %><span><%= digit %></span>
          </button>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="bench-balance" aria-live="polite"><span class="bench-sum" data-bench-sum><%= bench_sum(@sequence, first) %></span>
        <span class="bench-verdict" data-bench-verdict><%= bench_verdict(@sequence, first) %></span><% if @tally %>
        <span class="bench-verdict" data-bench-tally><%= bench_tallies(first) %></span><% end %></p>
      <p class="bench-edition" data-bench-edition><%= bench_edition(@sequence, @damage) %></p>
    </section>
  <% end %>

  <% if grille? %>
    <% grilles = plate_grilles %>
    <div class="actions grille-actions">
      <% if grilles.size > 1 %>
        <div class="segments grille-choice awaits-script" role="group" aria-label="Which grille to lay">
          <% grilles.each_with_index do |grille, i| %>
            <button type="button" class="segment" data-grille-choice="<%= grille[:part] %>" aria-pressed="<%= i.zero? %>"><span class="segment-title"><%= grille[:part] == :abbot ? 'Abbot' : 'Novice' %></span></button>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary awaits-script" data-action="lay-grille" aria-pressed="false">Lay the grille</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="download-stencil"><%= grilles.size > 1 ? 'Download the stencils' : 'Download the stencil' %></button>
      <% grilles.each do |grille| %>
        <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="copy-key" data-key="<%= grille[:key] %>"><%= grilles.size > 1 ? "Copy #{grille[:label].sub('grille', 'key')}" : 'Copy the key' %></button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <% grilles.each do |grille| %>
      <template data-stencil="<%= grille[:part] %>" data-label="<%= grille[:label] %>" data-path="<%= grille[:path] %>"><%== grille[:stencil] %></template>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <div class="actions">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" data-action="download-svg">Download SVG</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="download-png">Download PNG</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="copy-svg">Copy SVG code</button>
    <% if @layout == :rongorongo %>
      <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="turn-plate" aria-pressed="false">Turn the plate</button>
    <% end %>
    <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/">Inscribe another</a>
  </div>

  <form class="readback" method="post" action="/decode">
    <h2 class="index-heading">Read it back</h2>
    <input type="hidden" name="svg" value="<%= @svg_content %>">
    <% if grille? %><input type="hidden" name="grille" value="<%= @layout %>"><% end %>
    <div class="readback-row">
      <% if @secret %>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="readback-passphrase">Passphrase</label>
          <div class="passphrase">
            <input type="password" id="readback-passphrase" name="passphrase" autocomplete="current-password"
                   autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" required>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Decode this plate</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
